        rdfs:comment                   "Man's summer suit consisting of coat, waistcoat and breeches, beige silk, British, 1770-1779."@en , "A man’s summer suit, comprising coat, waistcoat and breeches, made of beige silk taffeta.  The coat has a 1-inch (2.5 cm) standing collar, and curving two-piece sleeves ending in a 3½-inch (9 cm) cuff.  The fronts curve from neck to hem with 3¼-inch (8.3 cm) pleats below the hip set at the side back.  Each front has a pocket with scalloped pocket flap; the centre-back seam is open below the hip.  The coat is unlined; exposed seams are backstitched and felled. The fronts are faced, and the skirts, collar and pocket flaps lined with carnation-pink silk taffeta, the pockets with bleached linen.    There are 10 worked buttonholes along the left front and 10 corresponding buttons, covered with beige silk and thread on the right, 1 at the top and 1 at the hem of the pleats.\n\nThe waistcoat is made of beige silk taffeta with a round neck, curving fronts, skirts reaching between the middle and top of the thigh and curving 2-piece sleeves.  Each front has a pocket and scalloped pocket flap.  The waistcoat is unlined; exposed seams are backstitched and felled.  The fronts and cuff openings are faced, and the skirts and pocket flaps lined with carnation-pink silk taffeta. There are 12 worked buttonholes along the left front and on each sleeve; 12 corresponding silk and thread-covered buttons on the right front and 1 on each sleeve.  \n\nThe breeches comprise 2 fronts, two backs and 2 waistbands, made of beige silk taffeta.  The back legs are cut higher than the fronts and gathered into the back of the waistbands.  There is a watch pocket in the lining of the right front waistbands.  The fronts close with buttoned waistbands and a fall front; the back waistbands with eyelets.  The breeches are unlined; exposed seams (except the outside leg) are backstitched and felled.  There are 2 silk and thread-covered buttons on the waistband, 1 on each front side, corresponding to 2 buttonholes on the waistband and 3 on the fall front.  Five buttons and buttonholes fasten each outside leg, with a knee-band below."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/88830ad2-397f-3bfb-98a8-af2491ada0da> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/572724aa-1d9a-3ae8-a932-d06ad3e13a3b> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/ae6016dc-8b23-307f-9558-1e37c75afd08> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/b5ce7dcd-2122-385a-9315-11d7c3fa832e> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/79fdfd7b-77fb-3c99-9976-07cba9cbdb33> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/27cf224b-9262-3bc5-8e2c-79c11d6b88d5> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/d8d36102-9449-3c1c-83f1-5748177274b3> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/4af093e7-e53c-3d42-a4bd-9dd2508f0377> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/f15717f5-a1b0-3574-9796-ea687c6e8e5c> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Man's summer suit consisting of coat, waistcoat and breeches, beige silk, British, 1770-1779."@en , "A man’s summer suit, comprising coat, waistcoat and breeches, made of beige silk taffeta.  The coat has a 1-inch (2.5 cm) standing collar, and curving two-piece sleeves ending in a 3½-inch (9 cm) cuff.  The fronts curve from neck to hem with 3¼-inch (8.3 cm) pleats below the hip set at the side back.  Each front has a pocket with scalloped pocket flap; the centre-back seam is open below the hip.  The coat is unlined; exposed seams are backstitched and felled. The fronts are faced, and the skirts, collar and pocket flaps lined with carnation-pink silk taffeta, the pockets with bleached linen.    There are 10 worked buttonholes along the left front and 10 corresponding buttons, covered with beige silk and thread on the right, 1 at the top and 1 at the hem of the pleats.\n\nThe waistcoat is made of beige silk taffeta with a round neck, curving fronts, skirts reaching between the middle and top of the thigh and curving 2-piece sleeves.  Each front has a pocket and scalloped pocket flap.  The waistcoat is unlined; exposed seams are backstitched and felled.  The fronts and cuff openings are faced, and the skirts and pocket flaps lined with carnation-pink silk taffeta. There are 12 worked buttonholes along the left front and on each sleeve; 12 corresponding silk and thread-covered buttons on the right front and 1 on each sleeve.  \n\nThe breeches comprise 2 fronts, two backs and 2 waistbands, made of beige silk taffeta.  The back legs are cut higher than the fronts and gathered into the back of the waistbands.  There is a watch pocket in the lining of the right front waistbands.  The fronts close with buttoned waistbands and a fall front; the back waistbands with eyelets.  The breeches are unlined; exposed seams (except the outside leg) are backstitched and felled.  There are 2 silk and thread-covered buttons on the waistband, 1 on ea